.TH "YAMLR-HEAL" "1" "May 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
yamlr-heal \- Propose repairs and remediate Kubernetes manifests.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBPropose Repairs (Safe-by-default)\fR
.PP
The \fBheal\fR command is the core of Yamlr. It proposes repairs for syntax errors, schema violations, and logic issues in your Kubernetes manifests.
.PP
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.RS
yamlr heal [PATH]... [FLAGS]
.RE
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Scans target files and applies fixers.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fBInteractive Mode\fR: Prompts before writing unless \fB-y\fR is used.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fBAtomic Writes\fR: Prevents data loss during writes.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fBBackups\fR: Created in \fB.yamlr/backups/\fR automatically.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fBType Healing\fR [Pro]: Structural type mismatch repair.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fBReferential Alignment\fR: Fixes broken ConfigMap/Secret/PVC references.
.IP "\fBIMPORTANT:\fR" 4
\fBFree Tier Healing Limits\fR
.PP
Limited to \fB5 files per day\fR. \fByamlr scan\fR remains 100% free and unlimited!
.PP
.SH "KEY FLAGS"
.SS "Primary Remediation Options"
.TP
\fB--apply\fR
Apply fixes directly to manifests on disk (Default: Preview).
.TP
\fB--diff\fR
Show side-by-side diff of proposed changes.
.TP
\fB--dry-run\fR
Show forensic impact without applying changes to disk.
.SS "Targeting & Environment"
.TP
\fB--kube-version\fR, \fB--k8s-version <VERSION>\fR
Target Kubernetes schema version (e.g., \fB1.30\fR, \fB1.31\fR).
.TP
\fB--crd <PATH>\fR
Path to CRD manifests to ingest and validate against.
.TP
\fB--helm\fR
Audit & heal Helm values in-memory.
.TP
\fB--kustomize\fR
Audit & heal Kustomize overlays in-memory.
.SS "Policy & Tool Ingestion"
.TP
\fB--ingest-opa <PATH>\fR
Path to OPA Gatekeeper JSON report to ingest and auto-repair.
.TP
\fB--ingest-kyverno <PATH>\fR
Path to Kyverno PolicyReport JSON to ingest and auto-repair.
.SS "CI/CD & Pipeline Integration"
.TP
\fB-f\fR, \fB--output-file <FILE>\fR
Path to write report (SARIF/JSON).
.TP
\fB--exit-zero\fR
Always exit with code 0 (for non-blocking CI warnings).
.TP
\fB--push-telemetry\fR
Push anonymous ROI data to global dashboard.

.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/yamlr/yamlr/issues>
.PP
